1
00:05:22,857 --> 00:05:28,857
The most frightening thing about Jacob Singer's
nightmare is that he isn't dreaming.

2
00:10:45,714 --> 00:10:51,714
Jacob's Ladder is a drama, mystery, horror film directed by Adrian Lyne.

3
00:16:08,571 --> 00:16:14,571
After returning home from the Vietnam War, veteran Jacob
Singer struggles to maintain his sanity.

4
00:21:31,428 --> 00:21:37,428
Plagued by hallucinations and flashbacks, Singer rapidly falls apart as the
world and people around him morph and twist into disturbing images.

5
00:26:54,285 --> 00:27:00,285
His girlfriend, Jezzie, and ex-wife, Sarah, try to help, but to little avail.

6
00:32:17,142 --> 00:32:23,142
Even Singer's chiropractor friend, Louis, fails to
reach him as he descends into madness.

7
00:37:40,000 --> 00:37:46,000
Jacob, played by Tim Robbins.

8
00:43:02,857 --> 00:43:08,857
Jezzie, played by Elizabeth Peña.

9
00:48:25,714 --> 00:48:31,714
Louis, played by Danny Aiello.

10
00:53:48,571 --> 00:53:54,571
Michael, played by Matt Craven.

11
00:59:11,428 --> 00:59:17,428
Paul, played by Pruitt Taylor Vince.

12
01:04:34,285 --> 01:04:40,285
Geary, played by Jason Alexander.

13
01:09:57,142 --> 01:10:03,142
Jacob's Ladder is a 1990 American psychological horror film directed by Adrian
Lyne, produced by Alan Marshall and written by Bruce Joel Rubin.

14
01:15:20,000 --> 01:15:26,000
It stars Tim Robbins as Jacob Singer, an American infantryman whose experiences
during his military service in Vietnam result in bizarre hallucinations.

15
01:20:42,857 --> 01:20:48,857
The supporting cast includes Elizabeth Peña and Danny Aiello.

16
01:26:05,714 --> 01:26:11,714
Jacob's Ladder was made by Carolco Pictures ten
years after being written by Rubin.

17
01:31:28,571 --> 01:31:34,571
The film garnered a cult following, and its plot and special effects became a source of
influence for various other works, such as the Silent Hill video game series.

18
01:36:51,428 --> 01:36:57,428
A remake was released in 2019.

19
01:42:14,285 --> 01:42:20,285
The film explores themes of vietnam veteran, new york city,
post-traumatic stress disorder (ptsd), experiment, nightmare.

20
01:47:37,142 --> 01:47:43,142
The tone is dark and emotional and mind_bending.
